# Build context exclusion for `docker compose build`.
#
# Without this file Docker streams the entire repo (including
# state/postgres/ at mode 700 root-owned and the 1.9 GB models/ dir)
# into every service's build context. That:
#   - fails outright when buildx runs as the non-root host user and
#     hits state/postgres (EACCES on individual files)
#   - wastes minutes per build streaming gigabytes the Dockerfile
#     never COPY's anyway (models are mounted at runtime via /models)
#
# The list mirrors .gitignore but is more aggressive because the
# Dockerfiles only ever COPY from core/, backends/, services/, web/,
# and a handful of top-level files.

# Runtime state — root-owned bind mounts, no Dockerfile needs them.
state/
media/
logs/

# Model weights + compiled caches. Mounted into containers via
# BABA_MODELS_HOST at runtime; baking them into images would inflate
# every image by ~2 GB.
models/*.onnx
models/*.engine
models/*.xml
models/*.bin
models/cache/

# Python build artefacts (re-generated inside each image).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.venv/
venv/
.uv-cache/
*.egg-info/

# Node — node_modules belongs to the web image, not the host. The
# web Dockerfile installs deps fresh inside the container's libc, so
# any host-side node_modules is at best wasted bandwidth, at worst a
# native-binding mismatch.
node_modules/
web/node_modules/
.svelte-kit/
web/.svelte-kit/
web/build/

# Brand masters. Sources for tools/build_brand_assets.py, which runs on the
# host at authoring time — the shipped derivatives live in web/static/.
web/brand/

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Secrets + local env. CRITICAL: keep .env out of every image so a
# leaked layer doesn't ship POSTGRES_PASSWORD / BABA_SECRET_KEY / RTSP
# credentials. Services read env via docker-compose at runtime.
.env
.env.*
*.secret

# Documentation + git noise — neither needed in any image.
.git/
.gitignore
*.md
!CLAUDE.md
ROADMAP.md
ARCHITECTURE.md
LICENSES.md
README.md
deploy/

# Logs that may have leaked into the repo from past runs.
*.log

# Vendored Python wheels / sdists never belong in an image build context
# (installed from the index in each Dockerfile) — BABA-14.
*.whl
/*.tar.gz
